==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*husjaz}}. It is remarkable that the expected alteration between nom.-acc. sg. ''*-Ce'' and oblique ''*-CC-'' or ''*-rġ''- in ja-stems with light root syllables has only survived in this word and {{m|ang|here||army}}, when ''hyse'' only occurs in compounds and poetry. All other expected examples have leveled the paradigm in favor of the oblique cases: {{m|ang|bedd||bed}}, {{m|ang|cynn||kind}}, {{m|ang|hryċġ||back}}, {{m|ang|nett||net}}, {{m|ang|pytt||pit}}, etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ang-IPA|hyse}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|m|hyssas}}

# [[warrior]]
# [[boy]], [[young]] [[man]]
# {{lb|ang|in compounds}} [[male]]

